# Line endings are LF in the repository and LF in the working tree, on every
# platform.
#
# Git's default on Windows is to convert LF to CRLF on checkout, which is fine
# for source a compiler reads and wrong for every file this project compares
# byte for byte. Two of those already exist:
#
#   * tests/tui/goldens/* are rendered terminal screens, read in binary mode and
#     compared against what the widgets produced. A CRLF checkout fails all
#     fourteen of them on Windows and nowhere else — which is exactly what the
#     Windows job found the first time it got far enough to run its tests.
#   * libs/infra/schema/*.sql is read at build time and embedded in the binary,
#     so a CRLF checkout ships a different schema string than a LF one.
#
# `text=auto` still normalises to LF on commit; `eol=lf` is what stops the
# conversion back on the way out.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Rendered screens: never touched, never diffed as text.
tests/tui/goldens/* -text
